The bug is in `withClient` (db.js:11-16): it calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` resolves. If `fn` throws, the client is never released and leaks out of the pool permanently. Over an hour that leaks the whole pool down to 0 idle, exactly matching the log.

Fix:
```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

Raise `max` only after this fix, if you still see saturation under real load.

